🧱 OBJECT CREATION FLOW (MOST IMPORTANT)

Whenever you create a child object, Java follows this order:

👉 Parent instance block
👉 Parent constructor
👉 Child instance block
👉 Child constructor

1️⃣ super() or this() must be the first statement in a constructor
2️⃣ If you don’t write either → compiler inserts super()
3️⃣ Parent constructor always executes before child constructo

