2️⃣ Code as GENERATED by the COMPILER (conceptual)

⚠️ This is NOT real source code you can see —
it’s what the compiler behaves like internally.

class Parent {

    // compiler keeps this constructor as-is
    Parent() {
        System.out.println("parent 0-args");
    }
}

class Child extends Parent {

    // compiler AUTO-GENERATED constructor
    Child() {
        super();   // automatically inserted
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        new Child();  // calls the generated constructor
    }
}


